/*! Employee cost calculator · v1.0.0
 *  Self-contained. No dependencies. Replaces the marker link
 *  <a href="#employee-cost-calculator"> inside a Webflow rich text block (blog post or tool page).
 *  Built by tools/src/employee-cost/build.py, which inlines the data below. Do not edit this file
 *  in tools/ by hand: edit calculator.src.js and rebuild.
 *
 *  Model (plan approved 28.10.2026):
 *    Total = S + B + T (employee, first year) + H (cost of the hiring process)
 *    Every year after = S + B + T
 *    S  BLS OEWS annual wage for role, area and percentile.
 *    B  S x (insurance + retirement) / (wages + paid leave) for the role's BLS ECEC group. OEWS annual
 *       wages already pay for paid leave, so leave is never added twice. Supplemental pay (bonuses,
 *       overtime) only when the reader ticks it.
 *    T  Social Security, Medicare, FUTA, the state's average SUTA rate on its taxable wage base, and
 *       workers' compensation from the same ECEC group.
 *    H  SHRM 2025 cost per hire (median, or average as the high case) until the reader fills any
 *       itemized line; then the sum of the lines replaces it, because SHRM's figure already contains
 *       ads, agency fees and recruiter pay.
 *  Internal time is valued at the person's own S + B + T over 2,080 hours, at the BLS median.
 *  Lines with no primary source have no default.
 */
